  "details": "The physical USB webcam was working normally in VRChat prior to the incident. After experiencing a sudden drop to 1 FPS in-game (triggered by an external instance/avatar load) and having to force-close VRChat via Task Manager, the webcam completely stopped working inside the game, despite functioning normally in other Windows apps (such as the native Windows Camera app).\n\nSteps to Reproduce:\n\nUse a physical USB webcam while playing VRChat.\n\nExperience a severe frame drop / freeze (1 FPS) inside a world, forcing a hard close of vrchat.exe via Task Manager.\n\nRelaunch VRChat and attempt to select the webcam in settings.\n\nThe webcam fails to initialize or display a feed, while working fine in Windows.\n\nExpected Behavior:\n\nThe webcam should release its DirectShow/Media Foundation hook correctly when the process closes, or allow re-selection upon relaunch.\n\nSystem Information:\n\nOS: Windows 11\n\nGraphics API: DirectX 11\n\nDevice: USB Webcam",
